			"date": "2023-02-05T15:49:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fosstodon.org/@gyanreyer\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>gyanreyer</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> From where I am in my React learning, the Vue ecosystem is better than the React one in any possible area I can think about. And Vue itself is really enjoyable while React is an outdated monstruosity with a really poor design (at least compared to Vue) making it rather unproductive to work with.</p>",
