		{
			"id": "109814384141957873",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ZMYaro/109814383666447435",
			"author": {
				"name": "Z(achary) Yaro",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ZMYaro",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/522/204/707/850/632/original/46ebaf6b76d19348.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-05T22:01:56.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I feel like part of the issue is with the latter, there was something we were encouraging people to move *to*.  The anti-React posts that usually hit my feed either don't say much more than “don't use React,” or focus on one specific use-case, leading their comments to get filled by people to whom the proposed alternative does not apply 😕</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109814420125726186",
			"parentId": "109814384141957873",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/109814420125726186",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-05T22:11:12.722Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@ZMYaro\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>ZMYaro</span></a></span> perhaps part of the issue is that React was successful at overselling itself for *everything*—and if we are talking alternatives I’d rather not repeat the same mistake</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109814433464586649",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://c.im/@TimWardCam/109814431192910486",
			"author": {
				"name": "Tim Ward ⭐🇪🇺🔶  #FBPE",
				"url": "https://c.im/@TimWardCam",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/581/265/973/061/815/original/97cc06882948468c.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-05T22:14:01.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I long since gave up working on the web front end. I just can't be doing with learning a whole brand new half-arsed \"latest and greatest\" set of frameworks every few months. (And they always will be half-arsed until someone throws away the browser as we know it and starts again.)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109814479190126306",
			"parentId": "109814420125726186",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ZMYaro/109814479157734781",
			"author": {
				"name": "Z(achary) Yaro",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ZMYaro",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/522/204/707/850/632/original/46ebaf6b76d19348.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-05T22:26:13.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> I absolutely agree with that.  I just feel like anti-React posts would get more traction (and maybe not stop, but at least make it more obvious when someone is on a post xe is not the target audience of) if they did more to head off that pattern.  Framing things more as, “If you're using React for [use case], you should really consider switching to [better alternative],” rather than, like you said, framing (maybe unintentionally) one alternative as the universal replacement for React.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "109814482821094769",
			"parentId": "109814479190126306",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ZMYaro/109814482738363138",
			"author": {
				"name": "Z(achary) Yaro",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@ZMYaro",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/522/204/707/850/632/original/46ebaf6b76d19348.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2023-02-05T22:27:08.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Like, “If you're making a static site, you should consider whether you need JavaScript at all, let alone React,” or, “If you are using React for encapsulated components, you should see what you can do with standard custom elements now without the overhead of React,” or something like that, could not just tell people to stop, but point them to alternatives.  Like how it was, “Move from CommonJS to ESM,” not just, “Stop using CommonJS!”</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
